  "answer_text": "You can download the latest version of Python from the **official Python website**:\n\n\ud83d\udd17 **https://www.python.org/downloads/**\n\nThe latest version is **Python 3.14.5**, and Python source code and installers are available for download for all versions on the official site.\n\nPython 3.14.5 was released on **May 10, 2026**.\n\nHere are some highlights about what's in the Python 3.14 release:\n\n- **Free-threaded Python** is now officially supported (PEP 779), and the evaluation of annotations is now deferred, improving the semantics of using annotations (PEP 649).\n- **Template string literals (t-strings)** for custom string processing, using the familiar syntax of f-strings (PEP 750).\n- A new module **compression.zstd** providing support for the Zstandard compression algorithm (PEP 784).\n\n### Platform-specific downloads:\n- **Windows:** https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/\n- **macOS:** https://www.python.org/downloads/macos/\n- **Linux/Unix (Source):** https://www.python.org/downloads/source/\n\n> \u2705 Always download Python from the **official python.org website** to ensure you're getting a safe and authentic copy.",
